# Two calls that make something on the disk and RAISE when the host refuses, on node, Rust, Swift and Kotlin (term/compiler
# decision 021 point 1b, as ruling 1473 amends it). Answered WITHOUT awaiting, as [blocking.tree](blocking.tree) is.
#
# `make-folder` makes a folder and every missing folder above it (node's `mkdirSync` with `recursive`): a folder
# already there is no refusal. `write-new` writes a file only when nothing is at its path (node's `writeFileSync` with
# the `wx` flag): it answers false, and writes nothing, when something is there, a file or a folder.
#
# Any other refusal raises `failure`, its note node's own message, worded once by [failure.tree](failure.tree): each
# binding answers the refusal's code name (empty when carried out), the step as node's `syscall` names it (`mkdir`,
# `open`, `write`) and the host's text, as a list of text. Node names the path given in both, whichever folder of the
# chain refused (`ENOTDIR: not a directory, mkdir '/x/plain.txt/a/b'`).
#
# A new module, never a change to the total calls: `make` of [directory.tree](directory.tree) stays total, since live
# callers rely on it (home-folder.tree's `try-move` at every command's start), and [../file.tree](../file.tree) gains
# nothing, so the webview bridge stays as it is.
#
# Browser: there is no file system there, so this module has no browser binding.

mark unstable

load @term/base/native/{platform}/file/create
  find create-folder
  find create-new

load @term/base/file/failure
  find raise-file-failure

# the folder at `path` and every missing folder above it. A folder already there is carried out
task make-folder
  take path, like text
  like void
  save raw
    call create-folder
      read path
  call raise-file-failure
    read raw
    read path

# the whole text written as UTF-8 to a new file at `path`: true when it was written, false when something is already
# there (EEXIST, node's `wx`), and any other refusal raised
task write-new
  take path, like text
  take body, like text
  like boolean
  save raw
    call create-new
      read path
      read body
  fork test
    hook test
      call is-equal
        read raw/0
        text <EEXIST>
    hook hold
      send back, false
  call raise-file-failure
    read raw
    read path
  send back, true
